WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.767 --> 00:00:03.002
-We here at "Late Night"
don't always have enough time

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.470
to cover all of the recent news.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.971
So here with the recap
is one of our writers,

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:08.374
Amber Ruffin, in a segment
we call "Amber Says What."

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:11.610 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.481
-Hey! You guys,
things have been crazy.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:19.619
Okay, first of all, I heard
that Amy Robach and T.J. Holmes

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.221
from "Good Morning America"
were having an affair,

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:24.224
and I was like, what?

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.892
Then I read that they got
kicked off the show

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:28.728
and I was like, what?

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.798
Then I heard that their exes
are dating each other,

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.833
and I was like, what...

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.135
is "Good Morning America" doing?

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:38.771
Let all four of them
host together

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:42.241
and give us the chaos
we deserve!

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.544
Make that show
last 24 hours long,

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:48.881
bring in a couples counselor,
and let the Emmys roll in, baby.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.449
Then I saw that Beyoncé went to

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:52.251
the opening of
Taylor Swift's movie

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:53.719
and I was like, what?

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:55.255
Why?

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:58.057
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.292
Taylor is no Beyoncé.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:02.628
Then I saw that Taylor went to
Beyoncé's movie

00:01:02.628 --> 00:01:04.096
and I was like, what?

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:06.766
Then I read that they went
to each other's openings

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.968
because people are always
pitting them against each other

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:12.771
and they're sick of it,
so I was like, what?

00:01:12.771 --> 00:01:15.207
I've been doing that.

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:17.309
And then I vowed to stop.

00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:19.712
So then I read Taylor Swift
was named

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.449
"Time's" Person of the Year,
and I was like...

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.453
...what...

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.656
a lovely choice.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:34.159
Then I saw the Rockefeller
Center Christmas tree

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:35.194
arrived and I was like --

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.428
[ To the tune of
"O Christmas Tree" ]

00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:38.264
♪ What, what, what,
what, what, what, what ♪

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.300
♪ What, what, what, what,
what, what, what ♪

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.136
Oh, geez,
beautiful, loves attention,

00:01:44.136 --> 00:01:45.672
and as always at 30 Rock.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:49.008
Who are you, me?

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.444
Then I read everybody
was furious

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.214
because Chris Wallace
told Adam Driver

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:56.515
he was ugly in an interview.

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:58.618
And I was like, what?

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.886
So turns out,
Chris Wallace was like,

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:02.555
"You don't look like
the typical movie star.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.125
And would your career be better
if you were better looking?"

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.126
And I was like,
this is what happens

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:10.763
when you let older white men
talk to young people.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.064
Look, watch this.

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:14.767
Hey, Seth, what did you say
when you met my niece?

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.602
-Oh,
"Do you like Matchbox 20?"

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:19.338
-See? A bunch of mess.

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:21.207
What does that even mean?

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:24.676
Then I saw George Santos
joined Cameo,

00:02:24.676 --> 00:02:27.246
and I was like, what?!

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:32.551
My favorite messy diva,
George Santos, is on Cameo?

00:02:32.551 --> 00:02:34.520
What a perfect Christmas gift.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.325
So I bought us
all a little Cameo from him.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.794
-Hey, it's me, George Santos.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.262
Don't be giving me any money.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:46.232
If you do, I'll probably just
use it to steal another baby.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.867
Then that's on you.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:52.805
This is definitely me,
George Santos.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.107
George Santos play video games,
right?

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:58.511
-Then I heard Brenda Lee
recently celebrated

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.546
that her song "Rockin' Around
the Christmas Tree"

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.781
made it to the top
of the Billboard 100

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:06.619
for the first time since 1958,
and I was like, what?

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.855
Then I found out she was only 13
when she recorded it,

00:03:09.855 --> 00:03:13.492
and I was like,
what does a 13-year-old know

00:03:13.492 --> 00:03:16.128
about rockin' around
the Christmas tree?

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.430
Girl, you better have a seat.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.498
You're not old enough
to be rocking around

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:22.201
the nothing
with your lil' fast tail.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:25.237
Then during a town hall,

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:27.073
Trump was asked
if he got elected,

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.608
was he going to be a dictator?

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.243
And Trump replied,
"Only on day one."

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:33.579
And I was like, what?

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:36.449
The correct answer was "no,"

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.350
unless you're asking me
that question,

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.052
then the answer is "yes."

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:42.454
The citizens of Ruffinland
are required

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:47.260
to give me little kisses,
fear and applaud me, or else.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.995
[Bleep], you would love
to live there.

00:03:49.995 --> 00:03:51.598
You would never leave.

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:54.233
Then I heard that
it's Seth's birthday soon

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:55.968
and I was like, what?

00:03:55.968 --> 00:04:00.073
Then I heard he was turning 50
and I was like...

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.774
what?!

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:04.677
Because I assume his hearing
is starting to go.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:08.247
Seth, if you can hear me,
say Amber is the most beautiful

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:11.216
and talented writer I ever met,
and we should trade salaries...

00:04:11.216 --> 00:04:13.352
-I'm not saying that.

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:16.055
-He can't hear.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.791
Then I read that FSU
was left out of

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.426
the college football playoffs

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.294
even though they
were undefeated.

00:04:22.294 --> 00:04:23.829
And I was like, what?

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:28.268
This really affects me, because
I think those players at...

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:31.537
I want to say
Florida State University?

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:34.873
-Yeah, that's right.
-Worked really hard to win...

00:04:34.873 --> 00:04:37.844
like somewhere
between 10 and 15 games?

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.211
-Yeah, right again.
-Yes.

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:40.880
And they should
be commended for that!

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:45.184
So you gotta blame
the head of football...

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.219
Dan Marino?

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:48.754
-No. What?

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:50.657
-Shut up. I did my best.

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.825
Then the White House
delayed its ban

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.960
on menthol cigarettes
over concerns

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.331
that it will hurt Biden's
popularity with Black voters.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:02.068
And I was like, what?
The nerve!

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:06.772
How dare you be so loud
and so right?

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:11.277
Then the Oxford Dictionary
named the slang word "rizz"

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.812
as the word of the year.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:16.015
It means having style,
charm or attractiveness.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:18.150
Seth, you got any rizz?

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.318
-Shoot, this Rizz God

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:21.353
is slinging
these interviews on the daily.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.655
-Oh, dang!

00:05:23.655 --> 00:05:25.825
Maybe Seth does have rizz.

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:28.628
-I mean, not as much rizz
as Matchbox 20, but --

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:29.729
-Never mind.

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.697
Guys, this has been
"Amber Says What."

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:34.399 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:34.399 --> 00:05:35.934
-Amber Ruffin, everybody!

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.071
We'll be right back
with Kate McKinnon!

